{"availability":"available","full":"19Technologies/cranoly-mono","name":"cranoly-mono","description":"Cranoly Mono: a black and white, flat fork of Cranoly, the notebook for learning languages with flashcards written inside your notes. Installable, works offline.","category":"Education","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-07T19:19:21Z","updated":"2026-10-09T18:55:07Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://cranoly-mono.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://cranoly-mono.vercel.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T19:34:28.723Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T19:34:28.723Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T19:34:28.723Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T19:34:28.723Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A black and white fork of Cranoly, the notebook for learning languages. You write flashcards directly inside your notes, link notes together, and hear every word spoken. It runs in the browser on desktop, installs on phones as an app that works offline, and ships as an Android app."],"features":["Laid out like Apple Notes: folders on the left (All Notes first, then the Mind Map, Practice and the Dictionary), then your notes (pinned first, then Today, Yesterday, Previous 7 Days and so on), then the note itself.…","Select a word, then Flashcard or Link: no syntax to learn. Flashcard fills in the meaning (and the article) for you and saves the card to the note; Link turns the word into a link to the note of that name. On phones…","Wikilinks: [[Note]], [[Note|alias]] and [[Note#Heading]] render inline. Hover over a link to preview the note. Clicking a link to a note that doesn't exist yet creates it.","Backlinks, outgoing links, outline and a local graph in a side panel you can open from the note's toolbar.","Mind Map: every note as a small dot on a plain dark background (dark in both themes), coloured by its folder and sized by how many links it has. Tags and unwritten links can be shown as their own dots. Hovering a dot…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/19Technologies/cranoly-mono/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"18a61f50a9db4d82899a1f40e90c945620d7393a207cb6b1c60c845bb7dcb642","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T19:34:28.813Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T19:34:28.813Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A black and white fork of Cranoly, the notebook for learning languages. You write flashcards directly inside your notes, link notes together, and hear every word spoken. It runs in the browser on desktop, installs on phones as an app that works offline, and ships as an Android app.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/19Technologies/cranoly-mono/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"AI with your Claude login.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/19Technologies/cranoly-mono/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"api_key","status":"optional","text":"There's no API key to add and nothing to pay Mono: it uses your own Claude account. (Anthropic doesn't allow other apps to sign people in to Claude, so the note goes to Claude itself, and only when you tap Open Claude.)","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/19Technologies/cranoly-mono/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"documented","text":"Sync, through the folder: no account and no server.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/19Technologies/cranoly-mono/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"18a61f50a9db4d82899a1f40e90c945620d7393a207cb6b1c60c845bb7dcb642","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/19Technologies/cranoly-mono/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T19:34:28.814Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-09T18:55:07Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/19Technologies/cranoly-mono/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T19:34:28.815Z","hash":"18a61f50a9db4d82899a1f40e90c945620d7393a207cb6b1c60c845bb7dcb642","originalBytes":14769,"storedBytes":14769,"truncated":false,"sear